# EAS Build ignore — keeps the upload focused on the Expo app.
#
# Why this exists:
# 1. Without this file, EAS uploads the entire pnpm workspace and runs
#    `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile` at the repo root. That fails with
#      EACCES: permission denied, mkdir 'artifacts/api-server/node_modules'
#    because the EAS Linux worker can't symlink workspace deps into the peer
#    package node_modules dirs.
# 2. We keep `pnpm-workspace.yaml` so pnpm can resolve `catalog:` versions used
#    by the Expo app (react, react-dom, zod, @tanstack/react-query).
# 3. We drop `pnpm-lock.yaml` so pnpm runs a non-frozen install scoped to the
#    one workspace package present on disk (artifacts/square-voice-agent),
#    avoiding "lockfile out of sync" errors and the multi-package symlinking
#    that triggered the EACCES.
# 4. The Expo app declares `node-linker=hoisted` in its local `.npmrc`, so the
#    install runs as flat copies — no per-package symlinks at all.

# Force a clean, single-package install on EAS workers
pnpm-lock.yaml

# Other workspace artifacts (server, web, PWA) — not used by the Expo app
artifacts/api-server/
artifacts/voycelab-landing/
artifacts/voice-agent-pwa/

# Server-only libraries (square-voice-agent has zero @workspace/* deps)
lib/

# Caches and build outputs
node_modules/
**/node_modules/
**/dist/
**/build/
**/.expo/
**/.next/
**/.cache/

# Local environment and secrets
.env
.env.*

# Tooling
.git/
.cursor/
.claude/
.vscode/

# Logs and OS junk
*.log
*.tsbuildinfo
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Repo-level docs / scripts unused by the Expo build
CLAUDE.md
RAILWAY.md
README.md
railway.json
nixpacks.toml
start-all.bat
tsconfig.base.json
tsconfig.json
scripts/
